From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: start-up supervision and clock anchoring

Adds ao_avfoundation_startup.h and .c, the passthrough sink's start-up
handling. It is kept in its own file so the AirPlay behaviour can be tuned
without touching the rest of the sink.

- Supervision, at the end of each feed step: rate 1 once the stream holds
  a second of audio (or mpv reached end of file), without waiting for the
  item to report ready; engagement as soon as the item's clock moves; one
  recovery seek to the stream start when it has not moved by
  compressed-start-grace, or by the shorter compressed-first-start-grace
  until the output's first engagement (an item that is not ready yet gets
  up to the ordinary grace); after the seek, a further grace each time a
  slow source makes progress towards the start-up lead; then fallback to
  PCM.
- Anchoring, with compressed-anchor-start and compressed-anchor-resume:
  small reads, at most one every 100 ms, that hold mpv's audio clock while
  AVPlayer's playhead has not started moving, at start-up and for 2 s after
  an unpause. An unpause requests rate 1 again and records the clock it
  reads after that request; the line reporting when the clock resumes does
  not depend on the option.

The lines it logs ("compressed clock engaged after", "first start recovery
after", "playback did not engage", "native compressed playback did not
start", "compressed clock resumed after") are the ones Vivid reads.

